// Packed fp4 routes through the cube, and the operand contract the two matmul
// ops are held to.
//
// tla.mmad and tla.mmad_mx are both written by the user and neither is inferred
// from the other, so each has to reject the operands belonging to the other.
// That check lives in the frontend, which is why these cases fail while the IR
// is still being generated rather than while it is being compiled.

// RUN: not %python %S/Inputs/generate_mmad_ir.py mx-half-scaled 2>&1 | %filecheck %s --check-prefix=HALFSCALED

// HALFSCALED: lhs operand was loaded by tla.copy(..., scale=...)

// RUN: not %python %S/Inputs/generate_mmad_ir.py mx-op-without-scale 2>&1 | %filecheck %s --check-prefix=MXNOSCALE

// MXNOSCALE: lhs operand was not loaded by tla.copy(..., scale=...)

// The encoding of a packed fp4 tile is its element type, so the load and the
// matmul cannot disagree -- there is no second place for it to be stated. The
// two operands need not agree with each other either: the cube has a mad_mx for
// every pairing, so a mixed-encoding matmul is legal and names both types in its
// callee.

// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/generate_mmad_ir.py mxfp4-mixed-encodings | %tla_compile - -o - 2>&1 | %filecheck %s --check-prefix=FMTMIXED

// FMTMIXED: mmadmx_float4_e1m2x2_t_float4_e2m1x2_t_float

// Packed fp4 is microscaling-only: an unscaled fp4 tile has no L1->L0A/L0B
// route at all, so the frontend stops it earlier, at the tla.copy that would
// load it. That check is a Python-side one and lives with the other copy
// checks (tests/test_copy_lowering.py). For IR the frontend did not produce,
// tla-cube-region still names the missing scale block on the matmul itself.

// mxfp8 raises the L0A / L0B alignment to 1024. The frontend cannot enforce it:
// tla.allocate sees only the address space, and 512 is what every other L0 user
// gets by with -- an mxfp8 operand allocated at 512 is legal right up to the
// matmul. The element format is only known at the mmad_mx, so the check lives
// there. Packed fp4 keeps the 512-byte block, as the case above shows.

// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/generate_mmad_ir.py mx-misaligned | not %tla_compile - -o - 2>&1 | %filecheck %s --check-prefix=MXALIGN

// MXALIGN: error: 'tla.mmad_mx' op lhs must be 1024-byte aligned for an mxfp8 MX operand
// MXALIGN-SAME: but the tile is aligned to 512 bytes
